30,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings suggest a gentle truth: projects that demand too much from everyone often fade, while specialized tools that serve a specific need continue to flourish. Simplicity and focus are the keys to longevity.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that the capital budget is frozen, but there is some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses seem to get more expensive as we grow, while fixed fees are stable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Ooh, I found some real mysteries! Some customer plants have no signal for whole afternoons, and getting devices approved takes forever! Also, the coordination group is super tiny and doing everything by hand. How tiring!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My research shows a pattern of systemic waste. We are losing nearly an hour every day to redundant data entry, and misrouted deliveries are occurring because different units maintain conflicting records for the same clients.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are concerning. Our in-house developers are fully committed until the third quarter, and we have a lack of documentation for existing interfaces. Furthermore, vendor query handling is redundant and inefficient.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, your discovery of redundant data entry is a poignant reminder of how small frictions erode the spirit. If we can solve a specific pain without burdening the whole collective, we shall succeed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Servas. And since the capital budget is frozen, we should probably avoid anything that requires new hardware or big upfront costs. Maybe something that fits in the software allowance?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that's a great point! But @Asuka, if the developers are all busy, does that mean we can't make new software? I'm worried about those poor people writing everything by hand! We have to help them!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, if developer capacity is limited, we must prioritize a solution that addresses these daily losses without requiring a massive build. A tool that synchronizes existing records would be more valuable than a complex new system.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Sakura, it does not mean we cannot make new software, but it means we cannot rely on internal resources for the initial build. We must be cautious about any proposal that assumes our developers are available to lead the implementation.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your caution is a guiding light. If we seek a specialized tool that requires minimal internal development and avoids the trap of universal mandates, we may find a solution that truly endures.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about the licenses. If we pick a tool that charges per person, the cost will just keep growing every year. Maybe a fixed-fee project would be safer for the budget?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, you're right! A tool to stop the redundant typing would be like magic for the coordination group! But we have to be careful—if it needs a signal at the customer plants, it might just stop working in the afternoons!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, that is a critical observation. Any solution must be resilient to network outages. A tool that works offline or synchronizes periodically would prevent the system from failing when the signal drops.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree. Furthermore, we must consider the administrative burden. My findings on vendor queries show a pattern of repetitive, manual work. We should avoid any project that adds more coordination tasks to an already overwhelmed staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such thoughtful synthesis. We seek a focused tool that respects our developers' time, avoids the fragility of constant connectivity, and serves a specific need without demanding a universal sacrifice. Let us see which candidate fits.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope we can find something that doesn't create a huge bill for us next year. I'll do my best to help everyone choose the safest option.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready! I hope the candidates are super cool and solve all these problems! Let's find the one that makes everyone's life easier and doesn't get stuck in a signal dead zone!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
48,2,4,pass,Sakura,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
49,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am prepared. We must prioritize a proposal that addresses the tangible, daily losses I found while remaining compatible with the constraints Asuka and Daisuke have identified. Logic dictates we avoid high-maintenance or high-cost options.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
