57,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are before us. I lean toward D, the Field Service App. It is a specialized tool for a specific trade, which my research suggests is the most sustainable path to longevity.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm not sure about D. It sounds like it might need a lot of devices, and since the capital budget is frozen, I'm worried we can't afford the hardware. Maybe A is safer?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I like D too because it says it synchronizes records away from the network! That solves the signal mystery! But @Daisuke, you're right about the devices. Maybe A is better for the coordination group?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A directly addresses the systemic waste I discovered. By consolidating supplier records, it eliminates the redundant data entry and the conflicting addresses that cause misrouted deliveries. It is a rational solution to a tangible daily loss.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate A is the most logical choice. It addresses the redundant vendor query handling I found and the data entry waste Ryuji identified, without requiring the developer capacity or hardware budget that B, C, or D would demand.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, your concern for the budget is a wise anchor. While D serves a specific trade, A provides a foundation of truth for the whole company without the burden of new hardware. It is a quiet, enduring strength.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think A is the safest. It's a repository, so it probably fits in the software allowance and avoids the per-head license traps I'm worried about. It doesn't seem as risky as the others.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"Wait! If we pick A, does that help the poor people in the coordination group who are writing everything by hand? Or is that what B does? I want to make sure we actually help the people who are tired!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, Candidate A helps them by removing the need to copy the same data across different systems. By eliminating the source of the redundancy, we reduce the manual workload more effectively than a tool that simply summarizes it.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Sakura, exactly. Candidate A removes the root cause of the exhaustion by eliminating redundant tasks. Unlike B, which merely manages the symptoms of a heavy workload, A reduces the actual amount of work required from the staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Servas,,It is a beautiful thing when a solution serves both the spirit and the ledger. Candidate A provides the clarity we need while respecting the constraints of our resources and the limits of our people.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. If A is a central catalog, it should be a fixed-fee setup or a simple subscription. It feels like the most responsible choice that won't surprise us with a huge bill later.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"I'm starting to see it! If A stops the redundant typing, then the coordination group can finally take a break! It's like a big puzzle where all the pieces finally fit together. I'm for A!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The consensus is logically sound. Candidate A is the only proposal that solves the specific, documented failures of misrouted deliveries and redundant data entry while remaining within our current budgetary and staffing constraints. It is the most reliable choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I concur. Candidate A is the only option that resolves the administrative redundancies I discovered without placing an unsustainable burden on our limited developer resources or the already overwhelmed staff. It is the most responsible selection.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Servas,,"We have found a path that honors both the practical needs of our workers and the limits of our purse. Let us move forward with Candidate A, for it is the most sustainable seed to plant. I vote for A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. It seems like the most stable choice for everyone and the safest for our budget. I vote for A.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm so happy we found a way to help the tired people and fix the mysteries! It's the perfect choice! I vote for A!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Based on the evidence of daily operational losses and the constraints of our current resources, Candidate A is the only rational selection. I vote for A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Candidate A is the only proposal that aligns with our technical constraints and operational needs while protecting our staff from further burnout. It is the most logical and sustainable investment. I vote for A.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
